  "captions": {
    "diagram-evidence-architecture": "Evidence-only core and optional intervention path. Applications supply captured records and independently read observations; explicit verifiers produce state and origin receipts. A domain matcher qualifies custom assessment targets. Explanation does not execute tools or replay. Separately invoked research adapters may supply estimates with refusal records; evaluator-only truth is reserved for audit. Adapter declarations are trusted inputs, not authentication or guarantees of read-only behavior.",
    "diagram-timeout-retry": "Illustrative timeout-after-commit sequence for an exactly-one contract. The first effect commits before its timeout acknowledgement and the agent reports failure. A retry without idempotency creates a second effect; a retry with the same provider-scoped operation key and payload reuses the first effect. Final independent, complete readback covers the stability horizon before a definite conclusion is drawn. Times are illustrative, arrows show event order rather than causal necessity, and the provider behavior is a declared example rather than a real-service guarantee."
  },
